# .github/release-sync-ignore — T-5 release fulfilment scope for this repository.
#
# Read by release-sync and by templates/ci/check-release-drift.sh, always from the DEFAULT
# BRANCH, so a tagged commit cannot exempt itself. Exact tag names, one per line. No globs.
# The audit prints this list on every run: exempting is a recorded scope decision, not a
# silenced check.
#
# Scope decision (meetmate#8): this repository was recreated as a public repo on 2026-08-21
# and inherited 28 tags from its private history. The PUBLIC release history starts at
# v8.0.0, its first public release. Every v* tag older than v8.0.0 is listed below.
#
# The tags are NOT deleted and NOT re-pointed — the history remains walkable. They are
# declared out of scope for Release fulfilment because backfilling them would:
#   - publish tag messages whose "#N" references belong to the PRIVATE predecessor repo
#     (meetmate-dev), where GitHub would autolink them to unrelated issues here;
#   - hand the public Latest badge to a release candidate (16 of the 24 listed here
#     are SemVer prereleases; 13 of the 18 the audit calls RED are)
#     — see caty-ai/family-dev-handbook#120;
#   - publish v7.4.1-stable's mangled message as release notes: it contains literal
#     \n escape sequences rather than newlines, so the body renders as one run-on
#     line. (The TITLE is safe either way — the workflow falls back to the tag name
#     above 120 chars, and a bare `gh release create` titles from the tag name.)
#
# It also prevents a red run on the public Actions tab: v1-phase1-stable,
# v4-stable-deepgram and v4.1-lcm-optimized match the v* push trigger but fail the
# workflow's SemVer check. The exemption check runs BEFORE the SemVer check.
#
# Exemption is total, not RED-only: the ignore test short-circuits ahead of every
# other classification, so these 24 tags also stop producing the audit's WARNING
# lines (lightweight and non-SemVer shapes), which is why the count goes to zero
# rather than to 'GREEN with 7 warnings'.
#
# NOT listed, deliberately:
#   v8.0.0                 — the first public release; keeps its Release and Latest badge.
#   pre-ui-redesign-104    ) non-v* tags. Outside the tool's scope by definition;
#   pre-epic107-impl       ) listing them here would imply they were ever in scope.
#   pre-epic107-a7-impl    )
#
# Once the release-sync caller (meetmate#5 / PR #6) lands, anything tagged from v8.1.0
# onward is fulfilled automatically. That PR is NOT merged as of this file's creation,
# so until it does land, no tag in this repository produces a Release on its own.
# Do not add new tags to this file to skip a release; the correct way to ship without
# a Release is to not push a v* tag.

